# MCP Servers

This project configures MCP servers in `.cursor/mcp.json`:

| Server | Purpose | Auth |
|---|---|---|
| `laravel-boost` | Laravel app tooling | local |
| `firecrawl` | Web scrape / crawl / search | `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY` |
| `n8n` | n8n workflows (HTTP MCP) | `N8N_MCP_TOKEN` |
| `google-ads` | Official Google Ads MCP (read) | Google ADC + developer token |
| `google-analytics` | Official Analytics MCP (read) | Google ADC |
| `google-search-console` | Search Console SEO data | `GSC_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PATH` |
| `nanogpt` | NanoGPT (required for image generation) | `NANOGPT_API_KEY` |
| `github` | Issues, PRs, CI, repos | `GITHUB_PAT` |
| `stripe` | Stripe billing / payments | OAuth in Cursor |
| `slack` | Slack search / messaging | OAuth in Cursor |
| `cloudflare` | Cloudflare API (Code Mode) | OAuth in Cursor |
| `canva` | Canva design create / edit / export | OAuth in Cursor |
| `claude` | Claude Code / Anthropic docs | remote HTTP |

## Credentials

- Never commit API keys, bearer tokens, or Google credential JSON.
- Copy `.cursor/mcp.env.example` → `.cursor/mcp.env` for local notes, then **export** the vars (or set them in the Cursor / shell environment) so `${env:...}` in `mcp.json` resolves.
- `.cursor/mcp.env` is gitignored.
- For **Stripe**, **Slack**, **Cloudflare**, and **Canva**: open Settings → Tools & MCP and click **Connect** to complete OAuth.

## Prerequisites

- **Firecrawl / NanoGPT / GSC**: Node/`npx` + the env vars above
- **n8n**: `N8N_MCP_TOKEN` (URL is set in `mcp.json`)
- **GitHub**: PAT from https://github.com/settings/tokens
- **Google Ads / Analytics**: `pipx`, `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS`, `GOOGLE_PROJECT_ID`; Ads also needs `GOOGLE_ADS_DEVELOPER_TOKEN`
- After changing MCP config or env, reload Cursor MCP servers (Settings → Tools & MCP)

## Agent usage

Prefer these MCP tools for the matching domain - discover tools with GetMcpTools before calling them.

For **design work** (brand assets, social graphics, presentations, marketing creatives), follow `.cursor/rules/design-mcp.mdc`: use **Canva** and **Claude** MCP.

For **image generation** (raster AI images, not Canva designs), follow `.cursor/rules/nanogpt-images.mdc`: use `nanogpt_image_generate` and prefer cheaper image models unless higher quality is requested.
